WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.146
Week 18: Irregular Preterite and Meaning Change. report discoveries and attempts distinguish intention from outcome summarize a trip

2
00:00:09.146 --> 00:00:22.924
Operational objective. By the end of this section you can report discoveries and attempts, distinguish intention from outcome, summarize a trip. The focus is useful performance, not isolated terminology.

3
00:00:22.924 --> 00:00:32.411
Language system. Irregular preterite stems; ser/ir; dar/ver; conocer, poder, querer, and saber in completed contexts.

4
00:00:32.411 --> 00:00:39.957
Sound and delivery. Irregular endings without written accents; rhythmic contrast of short verb forms.

5
00:00:39.957 --> 00:00:49.490
Core principle. Notice meaning first, then form. Retrieve the new language aloud, compare it with the model, and repair one feature at a time.

6
00:00:49.490 --> 00:01:17.433
Model language. No pude entrar porque perdí la llave. — I couldn't get in because I lost the key. Fuimos al pueblo por otra carretera. — We went to the town by another road. Allí conocimos al nuevo alcalde. — There we met the new mayor. Supe la verdad esa misma tarde. — I learned the truth that same afternoon. Quiso ayudar, pero no tuvo tiempo. — He or she wanted to help but did not have time.

7
00:01:17.433 --> 00:01:27.438
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
